{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Atlas Stream Processing Lambda external functions and error semantics",
  "slug": "atlas-stream-processing-lambda-external-functions-and-error-semantics",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:98dbe26da67e72c5f53baad949e3414dde974f2ea6b4ee876ffafd2ac794ea38",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "0bb836e308511bac257c0716fc1de1a5e2abb9198da4a7538be9ba962e948e5d",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:2bda590742fdcdc43ae5ee87d81e820c8c8b185b2129f9a3572b1f19adf76c66",
      "text": "Datadog distinguishes invocation errors from function errors and explains that Lambda Errors counts function failures, excluding invocation errors. Monitor invocation failures separately when diagnosing ASP-to-Lambda execution. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/key-metrics-for-monitoring-aws-lambda/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:811accb910f44cfbca35874cc98fb8d8785192c546e12fa4b5aeb7852e071381"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:b8b6a3b1d898b549982a6adeb0ab8d062a12861bc069af03764cb09d09ec175f",
      "text": "onError defaults to dlq; ignore drops the affected document; fail terminates the processor. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/new-mongodb-atlas-stream-processing-external-function-support"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:c1576e145d9133ef7aa07cce174c29b589cc6e6823478c0a554a4f189457e53d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:16e97b9dcd33c3ecc8be4af8a4fbdcd55107ac9b0327e783f2fb9a43e39d36df",
      "text": "Payload JSON conversion failures or invalid final BSON objects go to the ASP DLQ regardless of onError. Invalid operator expressions instead fail the processor. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9ed31e2831f4b46e26ec063927b4713a624c86fd12b1e18d9fc706e30cfbe8bc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:88207777d56e8e96263e839c6af76cc173bd85c7bc16cf0871f300cf70859d87",
      "text": "After asynchronous acceptance, Lambda owns its event queue. Its documented default is two additional attempts for function errors, including timeouts; duplicates can occur even without an error. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)",
      "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_Invoke.html",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:7cf42c17ca88bbfbd67a542e03e02da2e98616cc0135ebfdb6b6ddabc96e567a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e2e7b4c8993bebbf3100a8212a11466bef286c07941ad9cb7b10e3b2ae6a0bb8",
      "text": "Configure Lambda-side failure capture for asynchronous execution: a Lambda DLQ captures discarded events, and an on-failure destination captures failed-invocation records. ASP onError does not catch those later function failures. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:26270727e78c9049a2b53a715954a8ff676e2ddc10bad0a3983880e02feca488",
        "ev:5bf6b3cbc3801cd7b151ed8d96fdeb896195bef9d278219cad1f67c0259f3b53"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e23ef605da714c8f13a1562af50f213ad1f20a91d4591c15382aeb69bc7a4b7c",
      "text": "Lambda asynchronous delivery can duplicate events even without function errors. Make external side effects idempotent; stream processing completion cannot establish exactly-once Lambda side effects. The latter is an inference from the documented invocation boundary. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_Invoke.html",
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4e9798fc6dad6ae2f5f6188aada8a589f40b7d4d768b4817e10060fc5ecf877c",
        "ev:7b67c8d3fd0903e1b1caa510bb3663d0d7605e6c06920318bab7647f089a2c69"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:94cba461b166bd37856e719e0580aa4657a9d4a8c31160e9b56731380c667523",
      "text": "ASP onError covers invocation API errors in both modes and Lambda function errors only in synchronous mode. AWS async invocation returns acceptance rather than function results. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_Invoke.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5b55eb5bc8bfe57a31c30aaea39958e9d9974ed0f85fb3998d611a5f6dda0d19",
        "ev:b7d9bb213f1d98f35c2a9f38e53ff50c341ad0e67002dbdb77faa954e39d1b8a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:645097c703bc0deb1ba8b9476dfc8291ed2573957c196c23cbeac3d6bd92995f",
      "text": "ASP retries potentially transient request failures; its reference specifies neither retry count nor backoff. This differs from Lambda-managed asynchronous execution retries. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:09e04a7e83e0fb52a894f567a0489398f643234577287c4c9cd1ff2d7571db47",
        "ev:a003d7f91cbb4d3da5fe385a3413c9086eb9f29c214e21e553db2bd67406df72"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:106d68d2e610aff14801fa5207900b5a94bb1a6d35391a821073720acba2c71d",
      "text": "The payload subpipeline supports $project, $addFields, $replaceRoot and $set. Lambda responses must be buffered rather than streamed. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3f3dd7e10d1f9e07afe43a505d0eed853ab8cf5ed43f2da855f56649052c948f",
        "ev:82bb4f7bf5de081f893e3496428164ba1ff4662135182a364e9ca30f1c2dc04a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e879bf27e61a71289c243547197c5f4e0d629dd27e0e93a114f57975316a062a",
      "text": "$externalFunction invokes AWS Lambda through a registered connection. Synchronous execution returns enrichment results; asynchronous execution continues without awaiting function completion. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/new-mongodb-atlas-stream-processing-external-function-support"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9bfb2b545fe2720b8df391d74cab2ff18fd4a3d6fd9e50de815dd6258bef6708",
        "ev:bb4e7e954f8b073b69595b03e8c0dddb1e14287831c35abf28d49c611c8db265"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fc7ec6ac976d1200e981345c8800d522e73bb28ddd28de7085dc4dde08c5a9e1",
      "text": "execution defaults to sync. as is required for synchronous nonterminal stages, forbidden for async, and unset for a zero-byte response. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3a3c5660b27832487eb8fb73a61c2738cfa54db483ec63204f14cf39faab2f39"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6d246ac765965807eb1c1465802f21bc58eaf01a219f1a06b3fbfd21b1ac281d",
      "text": "Lambda must share the ASP AWS region. IAM needs lambda:InvokeFunction and lambda:GetFunctionConfiguration; ASP reads the configured timeout to wait through execution. Only buffered responses are supported. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/sp-agg-externalFunction.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:90fe0a57e72918e697433932bf26cd2dbaafb640b87acae983cc78df06fa7e9e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:233ff83f137e392c382787d8fdbd748d917831af83c153ec93fdd3c146d349cf",
      "text": "Lambda Invoke HTTP success does not imply function success: synchronous function failures use FunctionError and the response payload. An accepted asynchronous invocation returns HTTP 202. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_Invoke.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:06eb52974eb0fc5e24ef753590825b52608084b1aba532f04493cad7d1977046",
        "ev:924ad5bc5cd1d6450b69c176947d3b7e9b4b5e9adab21019f270f6bcd9411624",
        "ev:d6259bb665d34078c12e26b9d50111e97c09edc1a90efecc05e8074e2d25dcbe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:9830fe2655d6e5cdae30d71b28325f70400b6d2b01536227726f87c2f9d50ca3",
      "text": "Datadog\u2019s monitoring guidance recommends watching Lambda Errors and dead-letter delivery errors and correlating invocation metrics with logs. This supplies Lambda-side diagnostic guidance, not evidence of an ASP incident. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/key-metrics-for-monitoring-aws-lambda/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:605684046ae52bb8ec1fdbaea5a0e55e638bb9dbf61217152c21cc51d9cc91d8",
        "ev:75132253b939ef842c53709fe13171ed22f443c4ff82fc65dce98c18d3081857",
        "ev:a421f0e901151998745dc6bb4ec95a0255570f3bbefb033d5fb9a3d6cefee087"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f24db9177decffded5f298e401ef86cabdf4e87eb2e0f6f13bdc2ab7ba605866",
      "text": "MongoDB\u2019s changelog dates $externalFunction support to 26 March 2025, while its introductory blog is dated 3 July 2025; the blog date should not be substituted for the documented release date. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/changelog.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/new-mongodb-atlas-stream-processing-external-function-support"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:7d8bb58345abe410c50f0daefef27391b74df2679d98f7285c70c4bc09cc7008",
        "ev:938e2472b70a6eae061711ea26ceee5af28bdfafedff724b9fbfb9a5f4b21de4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:24cfad8ef9c3245f9874021ac4b47e6c92e6436684acf9929bd0568e0816c7cb",
      "text": "The changelog records externalFunction parallelism on 5 August 2026 and Lambda Private Link on 19 August 2026. The Private Link guide requires its endpoint in the processors\u2019 region. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/changelog.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-stream-processing/aws-lambda-private-connection.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4466d4a5f8cbdedbfde871e1b8a0405525f8b639d3add51a517948a0b95ce381",
        "ev:8dadd28b97c09fb80f32f8a387e73e9f9232f0ac0186b029ab49f5a10d76b0d7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fc30e945d75607808eb429d5c17c7da92f4d8a02768ff6cb2e131f8319bae450",
      "text": "For asynchronous function errors, Lambda defaults to two additional attempts, waiting one minute then two minutes. These defaults are configurable; they are not an ASP retry policy. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)",
      "source_url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html",
      "also": [
        "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_Invoke.html",
        "https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/key-metrics-for-monitoring-aws-lambda/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
